  "response_text": "We have found the memory location required to store the thread\u2019s context and stored it into stackptr. The Cortex M4 architecture requires that threads use the process stack pointer and not the main stack pointer to keep thread contexts and the system context separated. As such, calling __set_PSP and passing stackptr to it is required to tell the microcontroller that this is the stack to use. If we don\u2019t do this, the stack pointer may point to an invalid memory location, triggering a hard fault in the CPU as it tries to access memory at an invalid address.\\n",
